    "problem": "The original temperature reconstruction for Byrd Station, Antarctica, had calculation errors and was based on less-reliable historical data, leading to an overestimation of the magnitude and significance of warming trends, which this paper aims to correct and update using newly discovered sub-daily observations.",
    "method": "To create a more robust temperature record, the authors recalculate monthly mean temperatures for 1957-1975 using newly discovered sub-daily observations and merge them with modern records to update long-term warming trends at Byrd Station.",
    "task": "The task is to correct and update a reconstruction of the near-surface temperature record at Byrd Station, Antarctica, using newly discovered historical data to provide a more robust assessment of long-term warming trends in the region.",
